<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eiríkr Hákonarson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">960s–1020s</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Eric of Hlathir, Eric of Norway, Erik Hakonsson, Eirik Håkonsson, Eiríkr jarl</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eiríkr Hákonarson, also known as Eric of Hlathir, was Earl of Lade, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and Earl of Northumbria, the son of Earl <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakon-sigurdsson">Hákon Sigurðarson</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heimskringla">Heimskringla</a> he commanded 60 ships at the Battle of Hjörungavágr in 986, where a Danish invasion fleet was defeated. Exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> when Óláfr Tryggvason took power in 995, he burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staraya-ladoga">Staraya Ladoga</a>, and in 1000 he joined King Sweyn and King Olof of Sweden to defeat Óláfr at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-svolder">Battle of Svolder</a>, capturing his ship, the Long Serpent. He ruled Norway with his brother Sveinn under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweyn-forkbeard">Sweyn Forkbeard</a> until 1012, then joined Cnut's conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and received Northumbria; he is not mentioned in English documents after 1023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eirikr-hakonarson.jpg" alt="Eiríkr Hákonarson" width="330" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Krohg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sigurd_faar_grid_av_eirik_jarl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In Denmark the jarl was the king’s deputy, as Ulf Jarl was to Cnut the Great, and when Cnut conquered England he made <b>Eric of Lade</b> earl of Northumbria.</blockquote><a href="/societies/vikings">Social Hierarchy of the Vikings</a></li></ul></section>
